            topicHabits:"Habits", topicDiscipline:"Discipline", topicStoicism:"Stoicism", topicDeepWork:"Deep Work", topicProductivity:"Productivity", topicFocus:"Focus", topicMentalModels:"Mental Models", topicGoalSetting:"Goal Setting", topicPerformancePsych:"Performance Psychology", topicBehaviorChange:"Behavior Change", topicConfidence:"Confidence", topicMindset:"Mindset",
            authorActiveSince:"Active since", authorArticlesWritten:"Articles written",
            authorSubtitle:"Founder & Editor-in-Chief of Motiva Hub. Building a sanctuary for the disciplined mind — one idea at a time.",
            authorBioText1:"Motiva Hub is not a content farm. It is a daily practice, written in public, edited in private, and tested in my own life before it reaches yours.",
            authorBioText2:"I started this site in 2019 after a decade of reading the same five books on habits, focus, and discipline — and noticing that nobody was turning them into a daily, edible practice. The gap between knowing what to do and actually doing it, day after day, is the gap this site exists to close.",
            authorBioText3:"Eight years into building systems for myself — discipline rituals, focus stacks, sleep protocols — I can tell you one thing: <strong>motivation is a visitor, discipline is a resident</strong>. And the resident always wins.",
            daysKicker:"FREE GUIDE", daysTitle:"30 Days of <em>Discipline</em>", daysPageSubtitle:"A free challenge to build unshakable discipline. One small act per day — transforms your life by the end.",
            daysStartDay1:"Start Day 1", daysDownloadPdf:"Download PDF", daysGetViaEmail:"Get via Email",
            daysWeek1Kicker:"Week 1 — Foundation", daysBuildBase:"Build the Base",
            pillarDaysText:"One challenge per day. No excuses.", pillarMinText:"Each task takes 5 minutes or less.", pillarLifeText:"One month changes everything.",
            day1Title:"Wake Up at the Same Time", day1Text:"Set one alarm. Get out of bed on the first ring. No snooze. Your day starts with discipline, not negotiation.", day1Action:"Challenge: Wake up at 6:00 AM tomorrow. No exceptions.",
            day2Title:"Make Your Bed", day2Text:"The first small win of the day. A made bed signals: I am in control. Admiral William McRaven was right — it changes the world.", day2Action:"Challenge: Make your bed within 2 minutes of waking up.",
            day3Title:"Cold Shower — 30 Seconds", day3Text:"End your shower with 30 seconds of cold water. It trains your brain to do hard things voluntarily.", day3Action:"Challenge: Turn the water cold for the last 30 seconds.",
            day4Title:"Write 3 Things You're Grateful For", day4Text:"Discipline is not just physical. Gratitude trains your mind to see what matters. Write them by hand.", day4Action:"Challenge: Before bed, write 3 gratitudes in a notebook.",
            day5Title:"No Phone for the First Hour", day5Text:"Your morning belongs to you, not to notifications. The first hour sets the tone for everything.", day5Action:"Challenge: Leave your phone in another room until 7:00 AM.",
            day6Title:"10 Push-Ups", day6Text:"Discipline lives in the body. Ten push-ups is nothing — but doing them when you don't want to is everything.", day6Action:"Challenge: Drop and do 10 push-ups right now.",
            day7Title:"Review Your Week", day7Text:"What did you do? What did you skip? Write it down. Self-awareness is the foundation of growth.", day7Action:"Challenge: Spend 10 minutes reviewing your week honestly.",
            daysWeek2Kicker:"Week 2 — Consistency", daysStackHabits:"Stack the Habits",
            day8Title:"Eat One Healthy Meal", day8Text:"You don't need a diet. You need one good meal. Cook it, eat it slowly, notice how you feel.", day8Action:"Challenge: Prepare and eat one nutritious meal today.",
            day9Title:"Read 10 Pages", day9Text:"Not a chapter. Not a book. Just 10 pages. Consistency beats intensity every single time.", day9Action:"Challenge: Read 10 pages of any book before bed.",
            day10Title:"Walk 20 Minutes", day10Text:"Movement is medicine. A 20-minute walk clears your mind, strengthens your body, and builds the habit of showing up.", day10Action:"Challenge: Walk for 20 minutes without your phone.",
            day11Title:"Say No to One Distraction", day11Text:"One notification ignored. One scroll session skipped. Every \"no\" to distraction is a \"yes\" to your future.", day11Action:"Challenge: Identify your biggest distraction and avoid it for 2 hours.",
            day12Title:"Plan Tomorrow Tonight", day12Text:"Write down your top 3 priorities for tomorrow. Wake up with direction, not confusion.", day12Action:"Challenge: Before bed, write your 3 priorities for tomorrow.",
            day13Title:"5 Minutes of Silence", day13Text:"Sit alone. No music. No phone. No thoughts — just observe. The mind that can be still can do anything.", day13Action:"Challenge: Sit in complete silence for 5 minutes.",
            day14Title:"Week 2 Review", day14Text:"Two weeks in. Are you consistent? Write down what worked, what didn't, and what you'll change.", day14Action:"Challenge: Review your progress honestly. Adjust if needed.",
            daysWeek3Kicker:"Week 3 — Challenge", daysPushLimits:"Push the Limits",
            day15Title:"Cold Shower — 1 Minute", day15Text:"You survived 30 seconds. Now double it. Comfort is the enemy of growth.", day15Action:"Challenge: 1 minute of cold water. Breathe through it.",
            day16Title:"No Complaining for 24 Hours", day16Text:"Zero complaints. Not about the weather. Not about work. Not about anything. Gratitude replaces complaining.", day16Action:"Challenge: Go the entire day without complaining once.",
            day17Title:"20 Push-Ups + 20 Squats", day17Text:"The body is getting stronger. Prove it to yourself. Double what you did on Day 6.", day17Action:"Challenge: 20 push-ups and 20 squats. No rest between.",
            day18Title:"Do the Thing You've Been Avoiding", day18Text:"That email. That conversation. That task. Do it today. Discipline means doing what needs to be done.", day18Action:"Challenge: Complete the one task you've been putting off.",
            day19Title:"Eat Clean All Day", day19Text:"No junk food. No sugar. No processed food. One clean day shows you what your body is capable of.", day19Action:"Challenge: Eat only whole foods for one full day.",
            day20Title:"Wake Up at 5:00 AM", day20Text:"You've been training for 20 days. Now wake up an hour earlier. Own the morning before the world owns you.", day20Action:"Challenge: Alarm at 5:00 AM. Out of bed on the first ring.",
            day21Title:"Week 3 Review", day21Text:"Three weeks. You're not the same person who started. Write down how you've changed.", day21Action:"Challenge: Journal about the person you're becoming.",
            daysWeek4Kicker:"Week 4 — Mastery", daysBecomePerson:"Become the Person",
            day22Title:"2 Minutes of Cold Water", day22Text:"You've come this far. Two minutes is nothing now. Your mind is stronger than it was on Day 3.", day22Action:"Challenge: 2 minutes cold shower. You've earned this.",
            day23Title:"Help Someone Today", day23Text:"Discipline is not selfish. Use your strength to lift someone else. A kind word, a helping hand, a moment of your time.", day23Action:"Challenge: Do one act of kindness for someone else.",
            day24Title:"30 Push-Ups + 30 Squats", day24Text:"Three times what you started with. The body follows the mind. You are proof.", day24Action:"Challenge: 30 push-ups and 30 squats. Feel the difference.",
            day25Title:"No Social Media for 24 Hours", day25Text:"One full day. No scrolling. No stories. No reels. You'll survive. You might even thrive.", day25Action:"Challenge: Delete apps for 24 hours. Reinstall tomorrow.",
            day26Title:"Write Your Future Self a Letter", day26Text:"Where will you be in one year? Write to that person. Tell them what you started. Tell them why.", day26Action:"Challenge: Write a letter to yourself, one year from now.",
            day27Title:"Fast Until Lunch", day27Text:"Hunger is a feeling, not an emergency. Skip breakfast. Eat at noon. Learn the difference between want and need.", day27Action:"Challenge: Eat only after 12:00 PM.",
            day28Title:"Run or Walk 5K", day28Text:"28 days of discipline led here. Move your body for 5 kilometers. You are not who you were on Day 1.", day28Action:"Challenge: Complete 5K — run, jog, or walk.",
            day29Title:"Teach Someone What You've Learned", day29Text:"Share one lesson from this journey with a friend, a family member, a colleague. Teaching cements learning.", day29Action:"Challenge: Tell one person what 30 days of discipline taught you.",
            day30Title:"Start Again — Day 1", day30Text:"You finished. But discipline has no finish line. Start again. This time, you know who you are.", day30Action:"Challenge: Tomorrow is Day 1 again. Will you show up?",
            daysGetPdfKicker:"GET THE PDF", daysDownloadTitle:"Download \"30 Days of Discipline\"", daysDownloadSub:"Enter your email and receive the free PDF guide — or download it directly below.",
